8 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\" id=\"E1-MJMAIN-2E\" stroke-width=\"1\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\">\n<use x=\"0\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAINB-78\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use transform=\"scale(0.707)\" x=\"859\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-2032\" y=\"583\"></use>\n<use x=\"902\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-28\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"1291\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMATHI-74\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"1653\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-29\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"2320\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-3D\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"3376\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAINB-66\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"3830\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-28\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"4219\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMATHI-78\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"4792\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-2C\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"5237\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMATHI-79\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"5735\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-29\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<use x=\"6124\" xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-2E\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span>\nHowever, just knowing where equilibrium points are is not enough: we\nalso want to understand <em>how nearby solutions behave</em> when we start\nclose to an equilibrium point.</p>\n<p>Roughly speaking, there are three qualitatively different behaviors.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>An equilibrium point <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"2.009ex\" role=\"img\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.255ex;\" viewbox=\"0 -755.5 1061.4 865.1\" width=\"2.465ex\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\">\\mathbf{x}^\\ast</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path d=\"M227 0Q212 3 121 3Q40 3 28 0H21V62H117L245 213L109 382H26V444H34Q49 441 143 441Q247 441 265 444H274V382H246L281 339Q315 297 316 297Q320 297 354 341L389 382H352V444H360Q375 441 466 441Q547 441 559 444H566